    "created_at": "2015-09-08T18:08:36Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-09-08T18:08:36Z",
    "body": "@annevk, how do you expect the html spec to use the final Response.url from fetch?  Are there any attributes that expose the final Response.url to script?\n\nI ask because it seems hard to distinguish between:\n\n1) a fetch that redirects and results in a different Response.url\n2) a fetch that is intercepted and results in a different Response.url\n\nI think window.location doesn't have this problem because it will use manual redirect mode.  But is there anything else that might expose the intercepted URL?\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
